target/
artifacts/

# The seed half of the corpus is tracked; libFuzzer's own finds are not. See
# the repo-root .gitignore for why this is written file-by-file rather than as
# `corpus/`, and `just fuzz-seed` for what installs them.
corpus/*/*
!corpus/*/seed-*

# `Cargo.lock` is NOT ignored here any more. This crate is its own workspace,
# so it resolves its own graph — and cargo-fuzz has no `--locked` to bind that
# resolution with, which left the fuzz targets free to build against a
# different `aozora` / `comrak` than the library they exist to fuzz, with
# nothing in the repo able to notice (DEV-293). Committing the lockfile is what
# makes the resolution reviewable. `just fuzz-build` exercises this workspace
# and cargo-deny checks its resolved graph directly.
